          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            When in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category of topological spaces
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+space"} compactly generated space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            between the mapping space and the cartesian product in that category. For general
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %h2#exponentiable_spaces Exponentiable spaces
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} category with finite products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+object"} exponentiable
            if the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \times -: C \to C
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^c: C \to C
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_exponentiability_i Theorem (Exponentiability, I)
            %p
              Let
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              be the category of all topological spaces. An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              is exponentiable if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo :
                    %mi Top
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times -: Top \to Top
              preserves
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
          %p
            This functor always preserves
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times -
            preserves all small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
          %p This condition, however, is not really any more explicit. More interesting is to characterize the exponentiable spaces in terms of a point-set-topological condition.
          %h3#corecompactness Core-compactness
          %p
            For open subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            of a topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ≪
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\ll U
            to mean that any open cover of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            admits a finite subcover of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is relatively compact under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is way below
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %strong core-compact
            if for every open neighborhood
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            of a point
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≪
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\ll U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is core-compact iff for all open subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≪
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \bigcup \{ U | U\ll V \}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+lattice"} continuous lattice
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_exponentiability_ii Theorem (Exponentiability, II)
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              is exponentiable if and only if it is core-compact.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} local compactness
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} local compactness
            is defined appropriately (for every point the compact neighborhoods form a neighborhood basis). For this reason, that core-compactness is also called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong quasi local compactness
            = succeed "-space" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mtext T
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{T}_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sobrification"} sobrification
            is locally compact (
            %a{:href => "#HoffmannLawson1978"}> Hoffmann–Lawson 1978: 300
            ), so for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober spaces
            core-compactness and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} local compactness
            coincide.
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is core-compact, we can explicitly describe the exponential topology on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
            (whose points are continuous maps
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+basis"} subbasis
            elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_{U,V}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            an open subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            an open subset of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            belongs to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_{U,V}
            iff
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≪
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\ll f^{-1}(V)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo ≪
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_{U, V} = \{f \in Y^X: U \ll f^{-1}(V)\} .
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are Hausdorff, then this topology on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
            coincides with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
          %h3#ViaConvergence In terms of convergence
          %p
            Exponentiable (i.e. core-compact) spaces can also be characterized in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter"} ultrafilter
            convergence. Recall that a topological space can equivalently be defined as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relational+beta-module"} lax algebra for the ultrafilter monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C2%29-category"} (1,2)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rel"} Rel
            of sets and relations. In other words, it consists of a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and a relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi U
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\colon U X \to X
            called “convergence”, such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi X
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi R
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_X \subseteq R \circ \eta
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\circ U R \subseteq R\circ \mu
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            are the unit and multiplication of the ultrafilter monad, regarded as relations. In the paper
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Pisani"}> Claudio Pisani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Convergence in exponentiable spaces
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1999/n6/5-06abs.html"} TAC
          %p
            it is shown that a space is exponentiable (i.e. core-compact) if and only if we have equality in the multiplication law
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\circ U R = R\circ \mu
          %p
            Some intuition for this characterization can be obtained as follows. Consider the standard non-locally-compact space, the rationals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            as a subspace of the reals
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is a rational number and that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_n
            is a sequence of irrationals converging to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            we can find a sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi z
                    %mi m
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z^n_m
            of rationals which converges to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi z
                    %mi m
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z^n_m
            form a “sequence of sequences” which “globally converges” to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            by the composite relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\circ \mu
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            by the relation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi U
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \circ U R
          %h2#general_exponential_laws General exponential laws
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is exponentiable, then the exponential law gives us an isomorphism of
            %em sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map(Y,B^X) \cong Map(X\times Y,B)
            for any other spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is also exponentiable, then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            yields from this a homeomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                    %mo ≅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^{X\times Y} \cong (B^X)^Y
          %p
            We now agree to denote by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map(X,Y)=X^Y
            the space of continuous maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_exponential_law Theorem (Exponential law)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y,B
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in B^{X\times Y}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi θ
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [(\theta f)(y)](x) = f(x,y)
            %p
              defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta f:Y\to B^X
              which we call the map adjoint to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %p The adjunction map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Map
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Map
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi θ
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi θ
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta : Map(X\times Y,B)\to Map(Y,B^X), \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\theta:f\mapsto \theta f
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-to-one+function"} one-to-one function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact and Hausdorff
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
              is continuous in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Y
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta : B^{X\times Y}\to (B^X)^Y.
            %p
              If both assumptions (on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
              is not only a continuous bijection, but also open, hence a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
          %h2#based_exponential_laws Based exponential laws
          %p
            There is also a version for based (=
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+space"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            then needs to be replace by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of the based spaces. Regarding that the maps preserve the base point, the adjunction map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            induces the adjunction map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Map
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Map
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Map
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_*:Map_*(X\wedge Y,B)\to Map_*(Y,Map_*(X, B))
          %p
            where the mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Map
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map_*
            for based spaces is the subspace of the usual mapping space, in the compact-open topology, which consists of the mappings preserving the base point.
          %p
            It appears that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_*
            is again one-to-one and continuous, and it is bijective if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is locally compact Hausdorff. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
            are compact Hausdorff then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_*
            is a homeomorphism.
